re afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[1,10,11,18]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[5]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[6,21]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[6]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[10,11,18]},{"id":"asher_337","name":"Asher","also":"Aser","summary":"Happy, Jacob’s eigth son; his mother was Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid (Gen. 30:13). Of the tribe founded by him nothing is recorded beyond its holding a place in the list of the tribes (35:26; 46:17; Ex. 1:4, etc.) It increased in numbers twenty-nine percent, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[11]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[16]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[18]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[26]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,2,3,5,11,13,14,21]},{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[5]},{"id":"dan_323","name":"Dan","kind":"Region","lat":33.24856,"lon":35.65252,"summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":20,"v":[5]},{"id":"assyria_111","name":"Assyria","kind":"Region","lat":36.50969,"lon":43.2282,"summary":"The name deri